1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:04,150
The world has fallen in love

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,820
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,110
I just want to understand you

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,490
Won't you open up to me?

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:26,630
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

6
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,960
Enough to make me cry

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:35,300
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,430
and put it all in tune

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,270
I lost sight of everything but my goal

10
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,940
and had something important fade away

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:58,200
Let's start all over

12
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:03,330
The world has fallen in love

13
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:06,580
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

14
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,170
I want to know everything about you

15
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,340
Won't you tell me more?

16
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,970
One inch feels like a million miles

17
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:20,890
as the days just seem to race by

18
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,310
I won't and can't ever forget

19
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,560
this brightest page of my life.

20
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,780
Man, our pitcher yesterday was terrible.

21
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:41,120
I couldn't believe it.
They should've just put me in like I—

22
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:44,250
We've got an idiot here.

23
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:46,080
Chill out. Relax, me.

24
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:52,210
But doesn't he seem thinner?

25
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:55,130
Hope he's getting enough to eat.

26
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,880
Why not adopt him if you're so worried?

27
00:01:58,300 --> 00:01:59,760
I can't.

28
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,310
I'll start to get attached if I take him home.

29
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:05,600
What's so wrong with that?

30
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:12,190
The more things you view as precious,

31
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:15,190
the more they weigh you down.

32
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:20,030
That's what he said the other night.

33
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:26,700
Then the scouts would come and I'd be off to Barcelona.

34
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:29,830
He looks like he's enjoying himself,

35
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:34,880
but does he really think nothing of school or his friends?

36
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:39,590
Mabuchi-kun really said that?

37
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:43,600
I think he spends most of his nights wandering around

38
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,560
and being with people he can't tell us about.

39
00:02:48,350 --> 00:02:51,810
Futaba-chan, you sure know a lot.

40
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:55,150
I happened to see him and decided to play detective for a while.

41
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:57,280
D-Detective?

42
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:00,150
He's messing around and neglecting his studies...

43
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:04,200
I wonder if he even passed his midterms.

44
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,740
You're right to worry about him.

45
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:10,250
I just overheard Mabuchi and Tanaka-sensei talking.

46
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,210
Oh, Kou!

47
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:16,840
That's Tanaka-sensei's voice.

48
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:20,720
What's happened to you?

49
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:24,640
Every one of your midterm grades was below average.

50
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:29,600
If you don't pull yourself together, you'll seriously get held back.

51
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:33,020
Whatever. I'll just drop out if that happens.

52
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,520
Drop out?

53
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,650
You can't...

54
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:40,360
You're definitely going to regret it.

55
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,860
Will I really?

56
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:49,160
Calm down, I was joking.

57
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,340
I think people who want to quit should just do it,

58
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,800
but not if I have to see Tanaka-sensei so sad again.

59
00:04:04,090 --> 00:04:06,050
That damn brat.

60
00:04:08,010 --> 00:04:12,480
Even if he was only joking,
I don't want to even imagine it.

61
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:21,490
After Mabuchi-kun spent all that time with us at the leadership course,

62
00:04:22,150 --> 00:04:25,240
does he really still not think any of it is precious?

63
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:34,620
I'm sure that Kou

64
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:38,500
must have his reasons for saying such depressing things.

65
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:41,920
That's what I think.

66
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:47,600
So from here on out, let's do everything we can

67
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,600
to make sure he can never say those things again.

68
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:52,850
Futaba-chan, you...

69
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,810
I think you've gotten prettier lately.

70
00:04:55,810 --> 00:04:57,810
Though you were cute to begin with.

71
00:04:57,810 --> 00:05:01,530
Huh, really? You're making me blush here.

72
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:04,900
Actually, I decided to put on some makeup today.

73
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:07,740
Well, look at that. You did.

74
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:09,620
Still...

75
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:15,210
I don't think that's the only reason.

76
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:20,090
So today we will review some ancient Chinese history...

77
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:24,050
"We'll have fun every time we hang out together."

78
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:27,260
That's what I want Kou to think.

79
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,470
How can I get him to be one of us?

80
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:43,900
Why are you glaring at me

81
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,660
I'm not glaring at you

82
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,410
Huuuh?

83
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,410
Ugly

84
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,410
You were trying to glare holes through me!

85
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,620
I'm not glaring at you

86
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:59,670
I said I wasn't glaring, baldy!

87
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:02,710
I'm not balding!

88
00:05:59,790 --> 00:06:02,710
Peach is the bald one!!

89
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:05,340
I'm not glaring at you

90
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:05,510
I said I wasn't glaring at you, baldy!

91
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,640
Peach

92
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,890
Let me see that.

93
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:26,280
Just go.

94
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,030
How'd it go?

95
00:06:31,030 --> 00:06:35,160
Idiot. Your stupid note got me in trouble.

96
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,160
What, it's my fault?

97
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:40,880
You're the one who called him a bald peach.

98
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,710
Well yeah, he's balding!

99
00:06:41,130 --> 00:06:41,880
Still there

100
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:42,880
Still there

101
00:06:42,710 --> 00:06:44,090
His baldness isn't the point.

102
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:43,880
Still there

103
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,590
Is it just me, or is your face different today?

104
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:55,810
I used a bit of makeup.

105
00:06:55,010 --> 00:06:56,470
For Kou's sake

106
00:06:56,520 --> 00:07:01,020
There's only one reason for a girl who usually goes natural to start using makeup.

107
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,770
Love, right?

108
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:06,730
Bullseye.

109
00:07:06,730 --> 00:07:09,530
Kou, you say something too.

110
00:07:09,530 --> 00:07:12,820
Don't get cocky, you're just Yoshioka.

111
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:17,660
And why are you talking like Doraemon?

112
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:21,710
When do you think Futaba-chan will be ready for lunch?

113
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:25,460
Might be a while, so let's just start without her.

114
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,250
Sure.

115
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,300
What's that?

116
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,630
Oh, this?

117
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:33,180
It's the CD Mabuchi-kun lent me!

118
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:34,140
You're just Yoshioka.

119
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:34,720
Shut it.

120
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,100
You're just Yoshioka.

121
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:38,060
Knock it off!

122
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:41,230
Kou, I'm gonna go hit up the shop.

123
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:43,480
Sure, I'll come too.

124
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,610
Don't run away!

125
00:07:44,610 --> 00:07:46,360
Tell it to my stomach.

126
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:50,820
No comment about the makeup, huh.

127
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:00,580
Kou, what is it?

128
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:12,720
It doesn't suit you.

129
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,350
You're terrible!

130
00:08:18,350 --> 00:08:22,100
Don't come back if that's all you're gonna say!

131
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:32,900
Kou, are you more of a croquette man or a yakisoba-roll man?

132
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:36,570
Huh? I guess if I had to pick, yakisoba.

133
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:40,410
Same here! There's just something about yakisoba on bread that gets me.

134
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:43,370
Mabuchi, haven't seen you around lately.

135
00:08:43,370 --> 00:08:44,420
Hey.

136
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:45,670
Friends of yours?

137
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:47,630
Former classmates.

138
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:52,050
I haven't seen them before.

139
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:57,470
Looks like you're fitting in with the normal class now. It's like you've always been there.

140
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:58,970
Yeah, thanks.

141
00:08:58,970 --> 00:09:01,060
Oh, you must be in the advanced-track!

142
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:04,850
Come to think of it, Kou,
weren't you there too last year?

143
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:08,150
I'd totally forgotten, man.

144
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:13,030
It's not like Mabuchi ever did well on our tests anyway.

145
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:15,030
The normals suit you a lot more.

146
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:19,280
All last year I was asking myself why you were even in our class.

147
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:25,080
I get it now. The only reason you made it was because you were related to Tanaka-sensei.

148
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:27,630
No wonder you couldn't keep up.

149
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:31,500
Your brother must be relieved you're where you belong now.

150
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,590
I bet.

151
00:09:32,590 --> 00:09:36,760
If you'd actually failed out of the advanced track, he'd be out of a job.

152
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:41,810
That's enough out of you.

153
00:09:44,730 --> 00:09:46,140
You piss me off.

154
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,690
We're just joking around.

155
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:52,900
Then your sense of humor sucks.

156
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:56,400
Calm down. What are you so angry for?

157
00:09:57,990 --> 00:10:02,330
Why wouldn't I get pissed off when someone trash talks my friend like that?

158
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:05,250
Let's go.

159
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,830
Why you!

160
00:10:08,710 --> 00:10:11,540
Damn those chickens.

161
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:13,210
Not so advanced if you—

162
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:18,130
Those guys tick me off...

163
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:22,390
I hate people like that with all my heart.

164
00:10:38,450 --> 00:10:41,200
I should give up...

165
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,080
Those two are already...

166
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:01,140
Makita?

167
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,140
Tanaka-sensei.

168
00:11:09,020 --> 00:11:10,060
What's wrong?

169
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:12,650
It's Mabuchi-kun.

170
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,150
Hmm? Did he do something to you?

171
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:24,120
Is it true that he didn't do well on his midterms?

172
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:28,000
I can't exactly give out that information to you.

173
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:33,130
Were you concerned about him?

174
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:36,710
A little.

175
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:42,640
Ever since he was a kid, Kou was one to hold it all in.

176
00:11:56,110 --> 00:11:57,150
But to me...

177
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:07,450
He kept coming to me, crying "Nii-chan! Nii-chan!"

178
00:12:07,450 --> 00:12:09,500
He relied on me without reserve.

179
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:15,960
Nii-chan, it really hurts!

180
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,500
Don't worry, you're doing great.

181
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:23,090
Just on me.

182
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:32,430
But he's got good friends who'll worry about him now.

183
00:12:32,430 --> 00:12:35,850
I'm sure he'll be able to do his best for you.

184
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:37,110
Don't worry.

185
00:12:38,610 --> 00:12:42,190
Head back to class now.
Lunch is about to end.

186
00:12:45,610 --> 00:12:46,530
Okay.

187
00:12:59,670 --> 00:13:00,670
Yuuri?

188
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:05,380
About Mabuchi-kun
and his grades...
Can't we do anything
to help him?

189
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:05,380
About Mabuchi-kun and his grades...
Can't we do anything to help him?

190
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:05,380
Futaba-chan

191
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:05,380
Makita

192
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:22,400
Mabuchi

193
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,870
Kominato-kun.

194
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:30,240
Yes?

195
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:33,200
Are you free this Saturday?

196
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,600
Who the heck is it...

197
00:13:51,470 --> 00:13:55,430
Hey, Kou? Where you at right now?

198
00:13:55,430 --> 00:13:59,190
Kominato? I'm home.

199
00:13:59,190 --> 00:14:01,400
Great, that's perfect.

200
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,690
Should we get this too?

201
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:04,650
We're having a study party at your house today.

202
00:14:02,690 --> 00:14:04,650
Yeah, let's do it!

203
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:06,860
I really love this flavor.

204
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:06,860
We'll be right over.

205
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,780
Bye.

206
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,290
What's he going on about...

207
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,090
Wait, did he say a study party... here?

208
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:27,090
Did I dream it?

209
00:14:27,630 --> 00:14:28,550
The lock!

210
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:32,680
Lock, lock, lock...

211
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:38,940
G'morning, Mabuchi-kun!

212
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,860
Kou's room is pretty big.

213
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:47,280
Yeah, and it's well kept.

214
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,860
Let's get started.

215
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:52,200
Did you make sure to hide all your indecent books?

216
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,120
You didn't leave me enough time to do anything.

217
00:14:56,870 --> 00:15:01,130
Oh, right. I brought the CD you lent me.

218
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:03,090
Thanks for it.

219
00:15:03,090 --> 00:15:04,090
No problem.

220
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:10,010
We'll be teaching you all of our best subjects.

221
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:12,470
Huh? Teach me?

222
00:15:12,470 --> 00:15:17,390
You heard her! We'll show those
advanced-track pricks what's up!

223
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:23,520
And apologize to Tanaka-sensei, too.

224
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,020
He was really worried about you.

225
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:30,240
Nah, forget it.

226
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,410
Get back up!

227
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:35,280
Even studying can be fun if we all do it together.

228
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:35,870
Easy to understand
Chemistry

229
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:35,990
Simple math

230
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:40,040
Look, I even brought chips!

231
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:43,170
He's not taking the bait...

232
00:15:43,170 --> 00:15:48,670
Mabuchi-kun only just woke up, so we can't expect him to get right into it.

233
00:15:48,670 --> 00:15:53,300
I guess so. We'll go ahead and start then.

234
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:56,680
Kou, come over when you're more awake.

235
00:15:58,430 --> 00:16:00,730
Hey, who's good at math?

236
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:03,940
Yo, I'm pretty solid at it.

237
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:07,110
Then maybe you could explain this part.

238
00:16:07,110 --> 00:16:09,490
Just leave it to me! Where's the trouble?

239
00:16:09,490 --> 00:16:11,360
It's over here...

240
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:14,160
Crap, they're so loud.

241
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,410
I need help with this one.

242
00:16:16,410 --> 00:16:18,370
Oh, me too.

243
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:20,080
Let me take a look.

244
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:22,830
Okay, I see.

245
00:16:25,130 --> 00:16:26,840
How do I start this?

246
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:29,090
For that one,

247
00:16:29,090 --> 00:16:31,760
you do this here...

248
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:41,270
Kominato-kun, stop it! You're getting crumbs all over the place.

249
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:43,190
They're all over our notes!

250
00:16:43,190 --> 00:16:44,730
Aw, crap!

251
00:17:01,910 --> 00:17:04,160
They're not consommé flavored.

252
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:07,130
Mabuchi-kun got up.

253
00:17:07,130 --> 00:17:09,460
Those are only for people actually studying.

254
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,050
Yeah, what she said!

255
00:17:12,590 --> 00:17:14,050
Fine.

256
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:18,930
Kominato, shove over. I need space.

257
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:24,690
Hey, don't push me, Kou.

258
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:28,650
Yay, Kou joined us!

259
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:32,780
The snacks must've done it.
Let's keep pushing!

260
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:35,400
Mabuchi-kun, we have chocolate too.

261
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,410
Oh, thank you.

262
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:40,330
So, what are you good at?

263
00:17:40,330 --> 00:17:41,240
Chemistry.

264
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:44,160
Not what I expected.

265
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,370
I get that a lot.

266
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,880
Then show me what you've got, Sensei.

267
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:54,800
I know he's just making fun of me...

268
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:59,090
Hurry it up already.

269
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:03,060
...so why does it feel so good? Am I a pervert?

270
00:18:04,430 --> 00:18:07,270
We can start with the problems from the midterm, okay?

271
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:09,100
Get to it or I'll fall asleep.

272
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:11,020
Hold your horses!

273
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:13,230
Um, Mabuchi-kun!

274
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:19,870
Could you get everyone some cups?

275
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:21,990
Yeah, sure.

276
00:18:21,990 --> 00:18:23,660
I'll be right back.

277
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:26,580
I'll find some example questions in the meantime.

278
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:47,270
Everything alright? Need some help?

279
00:18:47,270 --> 00:18:49,390
Oh, thanks.

280
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:53,020
They haven't been used in a while, so I decided to wash them.

281
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:55,360
I'll dry them off.

282
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,230
Thanks.

283
00:18:59,610 --> 00:19:01,160
You can use this.

284
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,160
Okay.

285
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:05,790
Here.

286
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:06,580
Okay.

287
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,630
Hey, Mabuchi-kun...

288
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:22,680
What do you think of Futaba-chan?

289
00:19:23,890 --> 00:19:24,680
Do you li—

290
00:19:28,390 --> 00:19:29,430
If he does...

291
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,350
Oh, sorry.

292
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:37,030
I couldn't hear you over the water. What was that?

293
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:42,030
If he tells me that he likes Futaba-chan, what will I do?

294
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:44,490
Makita?

295
00:19:46,790 --> 00:19:49,200
Sorry, it's nothing!

296
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:52,580
I'll take these up first.

297
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,460
Sorry, I kicked the bag!

298
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:58,760
You klutz.

299
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,260
I'll pick it right up!

300
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:02,930
Did you hurt your foot?

301
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:04,970
No, I'm fine.

302
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,900
Who the heck brought potatoes?

303
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:40,590
Those two sure are taking their time.

304
00:20:40,590 --> 00:20:42,220
I'm gonna go check on them.

305
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,970
Have fun.

306
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:51,980
Murao-sama, teach me English.

307
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,560
Fine.

308
00:20:58,650 --> 00:21:02,070
Kou? Yuuri?

309
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:07,490
Oh, there you are.

310
00:21:07,490 --> 00:21:09,490
What happened? I thought you'd be right back.

311
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,700
Also, where's Yuuri?

312
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,760
Don't worry about it.

313
00:21:29,810 --> 00:21:32,930
Did something happen with Kou?

314
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:43,530
Nothing at all.

315
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:50,280
Whatever it is, it's not "nothing at all".

316
00:22:00,670 --> 00:22:05,800
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

317
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:11,180
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

318
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:16,640
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

319
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:21,940
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

320
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:31,660
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

321
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:37,250
but it passed, as days tend to do.

322
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:47,800
The rails carry you away

323
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:56,060
leaving me alone on our usual path.

324
00:22:57,180 --> 00:23:06,690
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

325
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:15,410
so why can't I say them?

326
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:22,380
Why can't I?

327
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:39,940
NEXT TIME...

328
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:32,930
You know, when someone keeps dodging their questions,

329
00:23:32,930 --> 00:23:35,430
most people don't probe any further.

330
00:23:36,310 --> 00:23:38,060
You're pretty incredible.
